    // "1,2,3" and a Dictionary, a tuple, a struct and an enum case all printed
    // "[object Object]", while swift-to-llvm-ir.abnf handed the raw value to the
    // shared println and printed Go's %v form (`<nil>`, `[1 2 3]`, a map with a
    // raw pointer address in it). Real Swift prints
    //   nil / [1, 2, 3] / ["x": 1] / (x: 1, y: "s") / P(x: 1, y: 2) / a(1, "x")
    // (verified against swift 6.1.2). The Go twin of this renderer is swRender in
    // abnf/jsrtswift.go; ./test.sh --cross diffs the two, so they must stay in step.
    //
    // Deliberate simplifications, shared by both halves: a class instance prints
    // as its BARE type name (real Swift qualifies it with the module, which this
