    //     a {__flo} box                  ==  a Double (or a Float)
    //
    // The residual "a fractional plain number counts as a Double" test is kept as a
    // safety net for any value that reaches arithmetic without having been boxed.
    //
    // DELIBERATE SIMPLIFICATION, both halves: Float is an ALIAS of Double, i.e. it
    // is modelled at 64 bit precision. Every value both types hold exactly gives
    // the same answer and the same text; a computation that LOSES precision does
    // not - real swift prints `Float(1) / Float(3)` as 0.33333334 and this prints
    // 0.3333333333333333. Modelling the 32 bit width honestly needs float32
